From e465457acaaafdf530acbbf0e150dc1a5a4c0d63 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Magnus Lindholm <linmag7@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 14:05:33 +0200
Subject: [RFC PATCH 12/17] sparc64: test masked Oberon routing to another CPU

Allow one destination selection before initial capture while IMAP is
invalid and ICLR idle. Change only the ten-bit target field and verify
readback; restore the disabled mapping on failure and prohibit arming.
Record the receiving Linux CPU and hardware ITID in the deferred report.

JPS2 Common Specification 9.3.3.1-2 defines destination Interrupt IDs.
Oberon destination bits 30:21 follow the existing target helper; retain
controller selection because the prepared interrupt bucket relies on it.
Keep the experiment default-off with CPU hotplug disabled.

Signed-off-by: Magnus Lindholm <linmag7@gmail.com>
---
 arch/sparc/include/asm/irq_64.h |  1 +
 arch/sparc/kernel/irq_64.c      | 59 +++++++++++++++++++++++++---
 arch/sparc/kernel/pci_fire.c    | 68 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 3 files changed, 120 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

